Changes from the upstream work
------------------------------

Per section 4(b) of the Apache License, Version 2.0, the modifications made in
this derivative are stated here. The authoritative record is the repository's
git history.

Added:

  * The `com_ext` community plugin interface, comprising
    `crates/service/src/com_ext/`, `src-tauri/src/commands/com_ext.rs`,
    `src/lib/api/com-ext.ts`, `src/lib/com-ext.svelte.ts`,
    `src/lib/com-ext-workflow.ts`, `src/lib/components/ComExtPageRenderer.svelte`,
    `src/lib/components/ComExtAppFrame.svelte`, `src/lib/components/ComExtSlot.svelte`,
    and the `/home/com-ext/view` and `/home/settings/com-ext` routes. This code
    is new and is not derived from the upstream extension implementation.
  * `src/lib/declarative-workflow.ts`, `src/lib/declarative-page.ts`, and
    `src/lib/components/DeclarativePageRenderer.svelte` — the workflow engine and
    page renderer extracted from the two upstream files named below, so that the
    official and community interfaces share one implementation.
  * `scripts/pack-com-ext.mjs` and `scripts/build-com-ext.mjs`, `plugins/tools/`,
    and `docs/community-plugins.md` — a packaging tool, the first community
    plugin, and its authoring guide.

Modified:

  * `src-tauri/src/commands.rs` — the in-app updater's release feed now points
    at this repository instead of the upstream one. Left unchanged, an update
    would replace the installed binary with an official build and silently
    discard the community plugin interface.
  * `src-tauri/tauri.conf.json` — the content security policy allows `eval` in
    `script-src`, which is how a community plugin page runs the code it ships.
    Without it a plugin could only render declarative documents and could not
    compute anything. This widens what injected markup can do, and it is a
    deliberate trade for an interface intended for a private group.
  * `src-tauri/src/lib.rs`, `src/lib/feature-flags.ts`,
    `src/lib/settings-entries.ts`, `src/lib/navigation.ts`,
    `src/routes/home/+layout.svelte`, and the locale message catalogues —
    additive wiring for the interface above.
  * `src/routes/home/overview/+page.svelte`, `src/routes/home/settings/+page.svelte`,
    and `src/routes/home/files/+page.svelte` — each gained a mount point for
    plugin contributions: the overview and settings pages render a plugin panel,
    and the file browser renders plugin toolbar buttons, context-menu entries,
    and fires the document-open and download-enqueued hooks. All existing
    behaviour is preserved; every mount point renders nothing when no plugin
    contributes to it.
  * `src/routes/home/settings/com-ext/+page.svelte` — a plugin that requests no
    capabilities is enabled as it is installed, so adding one is a single step.
  * `package.json` — devDependencies and scripts for building plugin packages.
  * `src/lib/extension-workflows.ts` and
    `src/lib/components/ExtensionPageRenderer.svelte` — the declarative workflow
    engine and the page renderer were extracted into the three new files listed
    above, which the official and community interfaces now share. Both upstream
    files keep their existing public API and behaviour and are now thin adapters
    over the shared implementation. Extracting them was preferred to duplicating
    roughly two hundred lines of interpreter logic that would otherwise drift
    between the two interfaces.
  * Version metadata and `src/lib/changelog/CHANGELOG.md` were reset to this
    edition's own `1.0.0` release.

Deliberately unmodified:

  * `crates/service/src/extensions.rs` and its commands remain the upstream
    signed extension system, byte for byte. The community interface is
    parallel to it, not a replacement, and the two share no state.

